    "title": "Braylon Mullins, UConn Huskies, Shooting Guard",
    "text": "Add Video H.S. Scouting Report Evaluated 07/14/2024 Adam Finkelstein Director of Scouting Mullins proved himself to be one of the best long-range shooters in the country this spring and summer. He knocked down 47% of his attempts from three in 3SSB play, even on high volume, making 6+ threes per game. He has a fairly low, but still quick, release, that he doesn't even always fully extend on. He's a threat to make tough shots in transition, off screens, or the dribble. He also has very deep range, well beyond the college arc at this point. He complements his shooting ability with a good overall feel for the game. He's a solid passer within the flow of the offense, increasingly dangerous cutter, and the type of off ball weapon that coaches will run plays for at the next level. While his niche is behind the arc, he was extremely efficient around the lane too, shooting 60% on two-point field goals, and yet could get more aggressive punishing defenders for running him off the line. Mullins has good positional size at right around 6-foot-5. He's a solid enough athlete to get up and dunk hard with only a step or two of separation. Physically, his shoulders are a bit narrow, but he's just starting to fill-out his frame and already has clear toughness and confidence about him. The other area of the game in which Mullins is a true standout is on the defensive end. He's quick laterally, very active with his hands (1.4 steals per game), and competitive with a scrappy mentality. He's also not afraid to stick his nose into traffic and pull-out some rebounds, on both ends of the floor (3.6 rebounds per game). The bottom line is that when you have an elite shooter, capable of getting hot at any point, who is also a standout defender, with positional size, solid athleticism, and a competitive mentality….you have an elite national prospect. H.S. Athletic Background Braylon Mullins is a Shooting Guard from Greenfield, IN. Add Timeline Events Timeline 2025Jun 1, 2025: EnrolledBraylon Mullins enrolls at UConn Huskies2024Nov 13, 2024: SignedBraylon Mullins signs letter of intent to...Oct 23, 2024: CommitBraylon Mullins commits to Connecticut HuskiesSep 21, 2024: O. VisitBraylon Mullins officially visits Indiana HoosiersSep 14, 2024: O. VisitBraylon Mullins officially visits North Carolina... Braylon Mullins photo gallery29 images Add Photos",
